Also maybe background color: fill with a rectangle with background color (already canvas background is set via CSS). But we can fill a dark rectangle to see something else. We'll just draw player.

Add code for __game: after render (or after update) but before end of tick, we need to call a function publishState that sets window.__game.

Simplify: add function publishState() that sets window.__game = { state: phase, score, player: { x: player.x, y: player.y, visible: player.visible }, objective: "Tap to build charge and jump over obstacles." }. Then call publishState() at end of render or each tick after render.

